// Sends from two loops of a `for`'s body to the same field land as from
// one place: in the order of the entities, and for one entity of its
// turns, whichever loop sent them (Inputs/looped_sends_places.ent: f32
// fractions whose sums depend on the order). Each box's sum's bits as
// they come in that order, worked out apart (a loop's sends all after the
// other's would give 1155167812 and 1148332464 for boxes 0 and 2). The
// same on one core, on many threads, and with every loop on many.
// RUN: %ent run %S/Inputs/looped_sends_places.ent 2>/dev/null > %t.one
// RUN: %ent run --parallel %S/Inputs/looped_sends_places.ent 2>/dev/null > %t.all
// RUN: env ENT_PARALLEL_MIN=1 %ent build --parallel %S/Inputs/looped_sends_places.ent -o %t.par
// RUN: %t.par 2>/dev/null > %t.many
// RUN: FileCheck %s < %t.one
// RUN: cmp %t.one %t.all
// RUN: cmp %t.one %t.many

// CHECK:      1155167809
// CHECK-NEXT: 1036341193
// CHECK-NEXT: 1148332465
// CHECK-NEXT: 1047489265
